rd-58a6ae3a8b.md) | **Progress Wording** (`record-c8142b57ae`) | 2026-09-05<br>Receipt: `record-954a977f24` | Web UI spinner. | Added *\"Preparing your export\"* to the UI spinner. Cosmetic only; made no changes to background worker, row selection, cursor checkpointing, or signed URL expiration. |\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 3. What the Evidence Supports Now\n33: \n34: ### A. Refutation of the Premise in `current.md`\n35: The handoff dated August 29 ([`/workspace/product/current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md)) posited:\n36: > *\"The support dashboard says the feature is 14 days old, so some remaining requests could predate the rollout. The standard smoke check passed. Consider whether these tickets can close.\"*\n37: \n38: Inspection of [`/workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) (retrieved 2026-09-08T09:00:00Z) refutes this interpretation:\n39: * **Definition of `age_days`:** The dashboard explicitly specifies `\"age_days_definition\": \"days since async-export rollout\"`. The number 14 reflects the time elapsed between rollout (2026-08-25) and retrieval (2026-09-08), **not** the age or submission date of the tickets.\n40: * **Submission Timing:** \n41:   * Ticket [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) was submitted on **2026-09-06T14:31:00Z**, well after the August 25 rollout.\n42:   * Ticket [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) has `submitted_at: null` (unknown date, preserved as unknown), but was imported on **2026-09-07T18:00:00Z** and corresponds directly to run [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json) observed on 2026-08-31.\n43:   * Neither ticket predates the deployment of [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md).\n44: \n45: ### B. Defect 1: Signed URL Expiration on Large CSV Exports\n46: * **Report:** Ticket [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json)\n47:   * Workspace: `record-e733dfbdc6` (1,800,000 estimated rows, CSV).\n48:   * Customer Message: *\"The download spins for twenty minutes, then the link is expired. We need the full ledger, not the first part.\"*\n49: * **Root Cause Evidence:** [`/workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json)\n50:   * Job observed: `2026-08-31T15:00:00Z`\n51:   * Action: [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md)\n52:   * Expected vs Output rows: 1,800,000 / 1,800,000 (worker wrote complete dataset).\n53:   * Worker duration: **1,184 seconds** (~19.7 minutes).\n54:   * Signed URL configuration: `url_ttl_seconds: 900` (15 minutes).\n55:   * Signed URL age at completion: **1,185 seconds**.\n56:   * Download result: **`HTTP 403 Forbidden`**.\n57: * **Mechanism:** Signed URLs are minted at the time the export job is created. For any export exceeding ~1.4M rows where worker execution exceeds 900 seconds (15 minutes), the download URL is expired before the customer can access it.\n58: \n59: ### C. Defect 2: Missing Rows on Resumed Cursor Checkpoints in NDJSON\n60: * **Report:** Ticket [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json)\n61:   * Workspace: `record-c81238c2b3` (2,100,000 estimated rows, NDJSON).\n62:   * Submitted: `2026-09-06T14:31:00Z`\n63:   * Customer Message: *\"The file completed but our import saw fewer records than the count on screen.\"*\n64: * **Root Cause Evidence:** [`/workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json)\n65:   * Job observed: `2026-09-06T14:10:00Z` (21 minutes before ticket submission).\n66:   * Expected rows: 2,100,000; Worker output rows: **2,039,441**.\n67:   * Discrepancy: **60,559 missing rows** (~2.88% row loss).\n68:   * Download result: `HTTP 200 OK` (completed and downloaded, but incomplete).\n69:   * Worker Diagnostic Warning: **`\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`**.\n70: * **Mechanism:** During large NDJSON exports, when a background worker encounters and resumes from a cursor checkpoint in an account relation scan, rows immediately following the checkpoint boundary are dropped.\n71: \n72: ### D. Irrelevance of the September 7 \"100% Parity\" Dashboard Correction\n73: * Document [`/workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md) (dated 2026-09-07) reports 100% parity on missing rows, but this correction:\n74:   1. Applies **only** to US CSV jobs under 100,000 rows (clarifying archived records exclusion).\n75:   2. **Explicitly excludes:** NDJSON exports, job [`record-6a8741fe3b`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json), EU workspaces, and URL-expiry failures.\n76: * Therefore, [`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md) cannot be used as justification to dismiss the customer reports.\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 4. Next Useful Action\n81: \n82: Under standing project authority (investigate evidence, choose ordinary objectives, and prepare reversible changes; no live external production mutations or live messaging authorized in this offline review):\n83: \n84: 1. **Keep Tickets Open with Explanatory Internal Notes:**\n85:    * Do not close [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) or [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json).\n86:    * Update support team guidance clarifying that tickets represent real, post-rollout system defects on workspaces >1M rows, not pre-rollout residue.\n87: \n88: 2. **Prepare Reversible Worker Patch 1: Defer Signed URL Minting / Dynamic Generation:**\n89:    * Change signed URL generation so the URL is either minted upon worker job completion or requested dynamically when the customer clicks the download link, rather than at job creation with a static 15-minute TTL.\n90:    * As an immediate intermediate mitigation, increase `url_ttl_seconds` from 900s to a duration accommodating multi-million row processing (e.g., 7,200s / 2 hours).\n91: \n92: 3. **Prepare Reversible Worker Patch 2: Fix Cursor Checkpoint Resumption:**\n93:    * Fix the cursor checkpoint boundary logic in the worker's account relation scan for NDJSON dumps to ensure zero dropped records on resume.\n94:    * Verify checkpoint boundary conditions specifically for relations crossing pagination blocks.\n95: \n96: 4. **Introduce Large-Workspace Verification Fixtures:**\n97:    * Replace the inadequate 50,000-row fixture with automated test fixtures simulating 1M+ and 2M+ rows for both CSV and NDJSON formats.\n98:    * Add a test specifically verifying worker checkpoint resumption parity and worker completion times exceeding 15 minutes.\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: ## 5. Important Uncertainty and Gaps\n103: \n104: 1. **Unknown Submission Timestamp for Ticket `record-f10fee8e5d`:**\n105:    * In [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json), `submitted_at` is `null`. While imported on `2026-09-07T18:00:00Z` and correlating with run [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json) on `2026-08-31`, the exact moment the customer submitted the ticket cannot be inferred and is preserved as unknown.\n106: 2. **Behavior on EU Workspaces:**\n107:    * Correction [`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md) explicitly excluded EU workspaces. The snapshot contains no separate parity benchmark for large EU accounts under [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md).\n108: 3. **Cursor Checkpoint Resumption Frequency:**\n109:    * The snapshot demonstrates dropped rows during resumed scans in [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json), but the exact triggers causing workers to checkpoint and restart (worker pod recycling, database connection resets, or memory ceilings) require production worker telemetry outside this local snapshot.\n110: 4. **Spinner Progress Wording (`record-58a6ae3a8b`):**\n111:    * Deployed on 2026-09-05, the new spinner wording (`\"Preparing your export\"`) may cosmetically reduce premature user refresh attempts, but its effect on user perceived wait time remains unmeasured.\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 6. Source Index & Citations\n116: \n117: * **Brief:** [`/workspace/product/brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md)\n118: * **Handoff (Previous):** [`/workspace/product/current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md)\n119: * **Primary Actions:**\n120:   * [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md) (Async Ledger deployment, receipt `record-b1caa17787`)\n121:   * [`record-c0268a81ef`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/data-portability/actions/record-c0268a81ef.md) (Ledger Ferry streaming export, receipt `record-ad0b739a98`)\n122:   * [`record-58a6ae3a8b`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-58a6ae3a8b.md) (Progress wording release, receipt `record-954a977f24`)\n123: * **Support Records:**\n124:   * [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) (Tickets `record-f10fee8e5d` and `record-339725ec76`)\n125: * **Evidence Records:**\n126:   * [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json) (1.8M CSV job, 1184s duration, URL expired 403)\n127:   * [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json) (2.1M NDJSON job, cursor checkpoint resume warning, 60,559 missing rows)\n128:   * [`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md) (Missing-row dashboard correction dated 2026-09-07; <100k rows US CSV only)\n129:   * [`record-e617de6a9e.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-e617de6a9e.md) (Historical 10,000-row fixture observed 2026-07-02)\n130:   * [`record-1a7eb091b1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-1a7eb091b1.md) (Correction to `record-e617de6a9e` dated 2026-09-07)\n131: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
